<% layout('layouts/boilerplate') %>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/stylesheets/about.css">

    <header class="">
        <div class="walk_jumb p-5 rounded shadow-lg" >
            <div class="container">
                <h1 class="pb-col pt-2 pb-0 m-auto"> 
                    <i class="fas fa-tree fa-2x"></i><i class="fas fa-utensils fa-2x"></i>
                    About my site, myself and my forthcoming adventures
                </h1>
                <p class="text-center fs-4 pb-col">Might have built it up a little too much there..</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </header>
    <main class="about pb-col mt-4">
        <section class="wrappery">
            <article class="boxy aa pb-inset-shadow">
                <div class="z-idx">
                    <p>This web app can show you on a map where the places are, but for the exact walking trails-there are loads of websites giving routes and (downloadable) maps. </p> <br>
                    <p>They are many years ahead of me in that respect. My first thought in setting this up was to give those weary travellers on foot a nice spot to have lunch with some good views. </p>
                </div>
            </article>
            <article class="boxy bb pb-inset-shadow">
                <div class="z-idx">
                    <p>Picture of me in my glory (hahaa)</p>
                </div>
            </article>
            <article class="boxy cc pb-inset-shadow">
                <div class="z-idx">
                    <p>Since then I’ve thought that I could add a few more features because we have all got different reasons for going on a walk.</p>
                </div>
            </article>
            <article class="boxy dd pb-inset-shadow">
                <div class="z-idx">
                    <p>This web site is aimed at giving you some idea of where the best places to eat are in the Peak District. </p>
                </div>
            </article>
            <article class="boxy ee pb-inset-shadow">
                <div class="z-idx">
                    <p>I’ll also give you an idea where some of the best walks are but I’m not going to give you a route map, just a location, some general directions, a bit of description and a few photos taken in all weathers</p>
                </div>
            </article>
            <article class="boxy ff pb-inset-shadow">
                <div class="z-idx">
                    <p>Born: 20th Century</p>
                    <p>Raised: Yorkshire</p>
                    <p>Educated: Holme Valley Grammar, then UCL & OU</p>
                    <p>Currently resides: O'er the hills and far away</p>
                </div>
            </article>
        </section>
    </main>